GOVERNING MODELLING OBJECTIVE — DO NOT LOSE THIS
-------------------------------------------------
For this project, we are NOT trying to reconstruct the physically realistic
internal clearances of a manufactured 2170 cell. The target is to reproduce
the already-defined OpenFOAM–ECM reference model in STAR-CCM+.

The OpenFOAM–ECM case is therefore the reference definition for geometry and
thermal coupling. Where that model has ideal/shared contact, STAR should match
that condition as closely as its geometry engine permits. Do not introduce
realistic air gaps, liners, clearances, or contact imperfections unless they
already exist in the reference model.

In particular, the radial reference target is JR OD = can ID = 20.6274 mm,
i.e. zero radial gap / ideal contact. The previous 19.25 mm JR OD is not the
final equivalence target because it creates a 1.3774 mm diametral gap absent
from the reference case. The 20.55 mm variant is only a STAR CAD-feasibility
fallback/probe if exact equality is rejected; it is not the preferred model
value. If a finite geometric clearance is unavoidable in STAR, thermal
coupling must still be configured to reproduce the OpenFOAM ideal-contact
condition. Any interface/contact resistance should be introduced explicitly
as a controlled model parameter later, not implicitly through an air gap.

